  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "1v2: steer towards the board",
  "description": "Three groups: A attacks with a ball, X and Y defend. Place a line of cones a little in from the right board, from the penalty area up towards the centre line. The cone line is a boundary the attacker must not cross. A goalkeeper is in goal.\n\nA starts with the ball and skates towards goal. X and Y skate up in an arc towards the attacker, X first and Y a little later and deeper. They go with A and try to steer them out towards the cone line and the board. If A gets past X, Y takes over and X skates back into the rink on the inside. If A goes outside the cones, the defence wins. Rotation: A goes to X, X to Y and Y to A.\n\nVariant: move the cone line closer to the middle to make it harder for the attacker. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The defenders skate with the attacker and steer – do not charge straight in."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Do not start backing off too early; meet the attacker high up the rink."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Timing for the second defender: close enough to help, not so close that both are beaten at once."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If the first defender is beaten – skate back into the rink on the inside."
    }
  ],
